                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22a49799-6225-3546-ac4b-5bbbccda3bac",
                        "entry_id": "09dd79b2-3327-3df6-95d3-d0dae2c26291",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Garni au moyen d’une aiguille de dessins en relief d’or, d’argent, de soie, de laine ou plus souvent de coton."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Broderie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6416bdf1-0163-471f-8449-4edfe8bba3fa",
                                "sense_id": "22a49799-6225-3546-ac4b-5bbbccda3bac",
                                "text": "Mlahfa violettes, vert émeraude, rose vif, jaune citron, grenat, bleu de ciel, orange, rouges ou blanches brodées de fleurs et d’étoiles multicolores…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0b441846-53e6-4ea1-a2da-82baa33e156a",
                        "source_entry_id": "09dd79b2-3327-3df6-95d3-d0dae2c26291",
                        "source_sense_id": "22a49799-6225-3546-ac4b-5bbbccda3bac",
                        "target_lang_word": "embroidered",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "embroidered",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17ca814b-c341-35d4-873a-2896f73fa6a7",
                                        "entry_id": "01aac02f-7f7e-37aa-b62b-0fbf19b640ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of embroider"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "embroidered",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc543a68-1bd8-3ceb-979a-41bf7be389f3",
                                        "entry_id": "10b68df4-380b-3d97-9d8f-8f0eeb6ae4aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Decorated with embroidery; covered in decorative needlework."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20c37c4a-88eb-47d0-934a-f2300d6547bf",
                                                "sense_id": "cc543a68-1bd8-3ceb-979a-41bf7be389f3",
                                                "text": "The very embroidered arras, which hangs yon pavilion, is worthy to be observed; but the artificers here, who display their curious works in our native metals, deserve high praise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b040c4d9-9705-470b-b808-c6c36395193e",
                                                "sense_id": "cc543a68-1bd8-3ceb-979a-41bf7be389f3",
                                                "text": "Surely he has appropriated wome of what should be his wife's jewelry, for in that very embroidered cambric shirt of his sparkle three splendid diamonds set in dark blue enamel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7585bcf-47eb-4910-8e33-1b34fed1dc24",
                                                "sense_id": "cc543a68-1bd8-3ceb-979a-41bf7be389f3",
                                                "text": "Luis de Avila and Lope de Soria often mention her in their letters; so for example, Avila: \"I came to Correggio, where I had Luncheon. I saw Veronica in bed, with a very ornamental night-cap and a very embroidered coverlet.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd56cdbb-e171-3789-a677-8a387db08ef9",
                                        "entry_id": "10b68df4-380b-3d97-9d8f-8f0eeb6ae4aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Embellished; elaborate, especially when containing superfluous or fictitious details."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ca78a93-c01b-45fd-8d62-18452e092240",
                                                "sense_id": "fd56cdbb-e171-3789-a677-8a387db08ef9",
                                                "text": "The orchestration is effective and ingenious, and some of the recitative is sustained with a very embroidered accompaniment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86e2a6c5-e918-42ad-8efe-d71128180044",
                                                "sense_id": "fd56cdbb-e171-3789-a677-8a387db08ef9",
                                                "text": "The man of business at his desk, the mechanic in his workshop, the idler on his couch, the man of letters in his study, has but to turn for a brief interval to these Lives, and he will behold, for every period and age, the very embroidered and moving scene that he has been seeking to understand and to sympathise with, in a way, in so far as the effect and the cause are concerned, not unlike that which Shakspeare's historical plays, and Walter Scott's historical romances, produce upon the vivid imagination."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "932d7fac-e6ea-4af8-a398-c92ccf3fbaf1",
                                                "sense_id": "fd56cdbb-e171-3789-a677-8a387db08ef9",
                                                "text": "That is not a very embroidered account of an actual occurrence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
